Subject: winemac: Add autorelease pools to WineMetalSwapChain C
Author: Brendan Shanks (CodeWeavers), WineHQ commit 1300ec99c7ed7461df1d400257aa83165faf0069 (2026-09-28), applied verbatim.
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine.
Provenance: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/1300ec99c7ed7461df1d400257aa83165faf0069 (in wine-11.20). Applied after
0001-0025 to Wine 11.19, source tarball 73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f. Not submitted upstream by AnvilMac (it is upstream).
Why (AnvilMac, 2026-11-12): the WineMetalSwapChain C wrappers ran Objective-C without an autorelease pool, so
objects they autoreleased were kept until thread exit. Called when a window's Metal layer is set up (Vulkan and
Metal games), not every frame: a small leak.

From 1300ec99c7ed7461df1d400257aa83165faf0069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan Shanks <bshanks@codeweavers.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:10:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Add autorelease pools to WineMetalSwapChain C
 wrappers.

---
 dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
index 94fc3e7cb61..e15f7083a4b 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -3783,24 +3783,36 @@ - (void) dealloc
 @end
 
 id<WineMetalSwapChain> macdrv_create_view_swapchain(WineContentView *view)
+{
+@autoreleasepool
 {
     return [[MetalViewSwapChain alloc] initWithView:view];
 }
+}
 
 id<WineMetalSwapChain> macdrv_create_offscreen_swapchain(void* hwnd, CGRect bounds)
+{
+@autoreleasepool
 {
     return [[CAContextSwapChain alloc] initWithHwnd:hwnd bounds:bounds];
 }
+}
 
 CAMetalLayer *macdrv_swapchain_get_layer(id<WineMetalSwapChain> swapchain)
+{
+@autoreleasepool
 {
     return [swapchain layer];
 }
+}
 
 void macdrv_destroy_swapchain(id<WineMetalSwapChain> swapchain)
+{
+@autoreleasepool
 {
     [swapchain release];
 }
+}
 
 void macdrv_window_create_ca_layer_host_view(WineWindow *window, unsigned int context_id)
 {
